compoundT -- the compound assignments += -= *= /= in a new-road body (GO 4, SEQ 805, 2026-11-28; Tony's ruling on SEQ 804).

Every case is one action written twice with the same text: caNNO is read on the old road (incant/grammar), caNNN is marked
newRoad and read on kantGrammar. Per operator: a count by a count and by a number, a number by a count and by a number,
a string by a string and by a count, a list (a field with two attributes, handed in as argument) by a count; the operand
a name, a call (caThree) and an expression; and the operator closing a while (drawText's dtHops shape), with a turn
counter that ends a loop which would not end by itself. All lines go to stderr, the engine's own ERROR lines among them,
so the block after CAROAD old and the block after CAROAD new can be compared whole. The harness (genLadder/pop.sh) pins
that the two blocks are THE SAME, and pins a few values by name. Where the old road's own answer looks wrong the twin
still only pins agreement: this fixture fixes nothing on the old road. The table of what each operator does on each
kind is docs/compoundAssignTable.md, read off this fixture's output.

